---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
// TODO OWNER: personalise this page. Add who you are, your background with cars/tools, and a photo if you like.
// A real person behind the site is one of the strongest trust signals for readers and for Google.
---
<PageLayout
  title="About DriveTested"
  heading="About DriveTested"
  description="DriveTested publishes plain-English buying guides and reviews for car accessories, from jump starters to floor mats."
  lede="DriveTested helps drivers buy the right car gear the first time, with clear explanations, honest picks and no fluff."
>
  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>
    Shopping for car accessories online is harder than it should be. Listings shout huge "peak amp" numbers, every
    product claims to fit every vehicle, and many review pages simply repeat the manufacturer's copy. We started
    DriveTested to do the opposite: explain what the specs mean in real life, point out the trade-offs, and recommend
    a small number of products we'd be comfortable putting in our own cars.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cover</h2>
  <p>
    Roadside essentials (jump starters and tire inflators), dash cams, floor mats and seat covers, detailing supplies,
    organization gear, and vehicle-specific guides.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We explain how we choose and evaluate products on our <a href="/how-we-test/">How We Test</a> page.</li>
    <li>Every guide says whether its picks are based on our own hands-on use or on research (specifications, manuals and published independent tests).</li>
    <li>We update guides when products change, get discontinued or better options appear.</li>
    <li>We're reader-supported through affiliate links. Read our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who's behind DriveTested</h2>
  {/* TODO OWNER: replace this paragraph with your name and a short, genuine bio. */}
  <p>
    DriveTested is an independent site run by {SITE.author}. We're drivers first, and we write for people who want a
    straight answer, not a spec-sheet dump.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>Spotted a mistake, or want us to look at a product? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
